    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>Custom Login Endpoint allows site owners to access the WordPress login screen through a custom URL while restricting direct anonymous access to wp-login.php.</p>\n<p>Need custom development?</p>\n<p>Visit <a href=\"https://futuristicit.com/contact-us/\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">FuturisticIT</a> for WordPress, WooCommerce and other services.</p>\n<p>Features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Custom login endpoint</li>\n<li>Custom login logo</li>\n<li>Redirect direct anonymous access</li>\n<li>Lightweight and easy to configure</li>\n</ul>\n",
        "installation": "<ol>\n<li>Upload the plugin through Plugins &gt; Add New.</li>\n<li>Activate the plugin.</li>\n<li>Go to Settings &gt; Secure Login.</li>\n<li>Configure your custom login endpoint.</li>\n</ol>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"does%20this%20improve%20security%3F\">\nDoes this improve security?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>This plugin changes how visitors access the login page. It should not replace strong passwords, two-factor authentication, or other security measures.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"what%20if%20my%20custom%20url%20stops%20working%3F\">\nWhat if my custom URL stops working?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Visit Settings &gt; Permalinks and click Save Changes to flush rewrite rules.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release.</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "Replace the default WordPress login URL with a custom endpoint and customize the login logo.",
